circle-rp1dsi-warmrestart.patch (Sidecar): the Touch Display 2's touch controller after a warm restart (the engine's own reboot:
an update, a Wi-Fi join, a change of device). On top of circle-rp1dsi-fb.patch and circle-rp1dsi-td2.patch (build.sh applies
it after both). Taken from bandersong's sidecar-firmware PR #4 (circle-rp1dsi.patch), narrowed to the warm restart:
- CRPiTouchScreen2::PowerOff (and CILI9881Panel::PowerOff, CRPiTouchScreen::PowerOff): the panel shut down as Linux does
  before a reboot (display off, sleep in, reset, backlight and the touch controller's supply off). The engine calls it from
  StopAndReboot (pi/ui/sidecar_display.cpp PowerOff).
- At start the GT911's supply is switched off for a real power-on reset (100 ms, then 300 ms, then 1000 ms on each retry), and
  the controller is probed on 0x5D and on 0x14 (the address it takes after a reset with INT high) after each. The regulator's
  own init switches the supply off for microseconds only, which does not reset a GT911 whose supply the panel's MCU kept
  on. A controller that stays silent leaves the engine running without touch, as circle-rp1dsi-td2.patch does.

